module caed-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Eastern District of California's own civil periods, computed under
// FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule. Rules that state
// no period this layer can count stay out: the hearing date, which is a
// minimum (not less than thirty-five (35) days after service and filing of
// the motion, E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(b)), not a deadline; the initial
// stipulation extending time to respond by no more than twenty-eight (28)
// days, a cap on an extension, not a period (E.D. Cal. L.R. 144(a)); and
// the criminal and bankruptcy rules. The earlier E.D. Cal. outline's FRCP
// flow and its decisions (Eitel v. McCool, Twombly, Iqbal, Lopez v. Smith,
// Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Reeves, Catlin, Bowles v. Russell,
// Hamer) are FRCP and FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap; no
// reporter text is vendored, so they are removed here.
/// A motion is filed and served (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(b), (c)).
event MotionFiled()
/// An opposition to a motion is filed (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(d)).
event OppositionFiled()
/// A reply is filed (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(m)).
event ReplyFiled()
/// The scheduled hearing date of a motion (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(f)).
event HearingDate()
/// A motion in an action where one party is incarcerated and proceeding in
/// propria persona is served (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(l)).
event PrisonerActionMotionServed()
/// An opposition to a motion in such an action is filed in CM/ECF (E.D.
/// Cal. L.R. 230(l)).
event PrisonerActionOppositionFiled()
/// The date the court sets for the final pretrial conference (E.D. Cal.
/// L.R. 281(a)).
event FinalPretrialConference()
/// Judgment or an order under which costs may be claimed is entered (E.D.
/// Cal. L.R. 292(b)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// The bill of costs is served (E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(c)).
event CostBillServed()
/// Notice of the clerk's taxing of costs is served (E.D. Cal. L.R.
/// 292(e)).
event CostsTaxedNoticeServed()
/// Final judgment is entered (E.D. Cal. L.R. 293(a)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// A magistrate judge's ruling on a general pretrial matter is served on
/// the parties (E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(b)).
event MagistrateRulingServed()
/// A request for reconsideration by the district court of a magistrate
/// judge's ruling is served (E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(d)).
event ReconsiderationRequestServed()
/// A magistrate judge's proposed findings and recommendations are served
/// on the parties (E.D. Cal. L.R. 304(b)).
event FindingsAndRecommendationsServed()
/// Objections to proposed findings and recommendations are served (E.D.
/// Cal. L.R. 304(d)).
event ObjectionsServed()

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(c): an opposition, or a statement of non-opposition,
/// is filed and served no later than fourteen (14) days after the motion was
/// filed. A party that has not timely opposed is not heard at oral argument,
/// and the court may treat the failure as non-opposition. A related
/// counter-motion is due on the same date (E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(e)).
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(c)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(d): the moving party may serve and file a reply no
/// later than ten (10) days after the opposition was filed.
deadline reply-period: 10.days after OppositionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(d)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(f): a request to continue a hearing on the motion
/// calendar is made at least seven (7) days before the scheduled hearing
/// date; a continuance does not extend the time for opposition or reply
/// unless the court orders otherwise.
deadline continuance-request-period: 7.days before HearingDate() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(f)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(l): in an action where one party is incarcerated and
/// proceeding in propria persona, an opposition, or a statement of no
/// opposition, is served and filed not more than twenty-one (21) days after
/// the date of service of the motion.
deadline prisoner-action-opposition-period: 21.days after PrisonerActionMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(l)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(l): in such an action the moving party may serve and
/// file a reply not more than fourteen (14) days after the opposition has
/// been filed; the motion is deemed submitted when that time expires.
deadline prisoner-action-reply-period: 14.days after PrisonerActionOppositionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(l)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(m)(1): if the reply submits new evidence, the
/// opposing party may file and serve an Objection to Reply Evidence no later
/// than seven (7) days after the reply is filed.
deadline reply-evidence-objection-period: 7.days after ReplyFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 230(m)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 281(a)(1): with separate statements, the plaintiff serves
/// and files its pretrial statement not less than fourteen (14) days before
/// the final pretrial conference.
deadline plaintiff-pretrial-statement-period: 14.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 281(a)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 281(a)(1), (2): every other party's separate pretrial
/// statement, or a joint pretrial statement, is filed not less than seven
/// (7) days before the final pretrial conference, as the pretrial order
/// requires.
deadline pretrial-statement-period: 7.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 281(a)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(b): the prevailing party may serve and file a bill of
/// costs within fourteen (14) days after entry of the judgment or order
/// under which costs may be claimed.
deadline cost-bill-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(b)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(c): the party against whom costs are claimed may file
/// specific objections within seven (7) days from the date of service.
deadline cost-objection-period: 7.days after CostBillServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(c)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(e): the clerk's taxing of costs may be reviewed by the
/// court on a motion filed and served within seven (7) days after notice of
/// the taxing has been served.
deadline cost-review-period: 7.days after CostsTaxedNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 292(e)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 293(a): a motion for statutory attorneys' fees to a
/// prevailing party is filed not later than twenty-eight (28) days after
/// entry of final judgment, and is governed by E.D. Cal. L.R. 230.
deadline fee-motion-period: 28.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 293(a)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(b): a magistrate judge's ruling on a general pretrial
/// matter is final unless reconsideration is sought within fourteen (14)
/// days from service of the ruling, unless the magistrate judge or the
/// judge prescribes a different time.
deadline magistrate-reconsideration-period: 14.days after MagistrateRulingServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(b)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(d): opposition to a request for reconsideration is
/// served and filed within seven (7) days after service of the request.
deadline reconsideration-opposition-period: 7.days after ReconsiderationRequestServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 303(d)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 304(b): objections to a magistrate judge's proposed
/// findings and recommendations are filed and served within fourteen (14)
/// days after their service, unless the court prescribes a different time.
deadline findings-objection-period: 14.days after FindingsAndRecommendationsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 304(b)"

/// E.D. Cal. L.R. 304(d): responses to objections are filed and served
/// within fourteen (14) days after service of the objections.
deadline objection-response-period: 14.days after ObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Cal. L.R. 304(d)"
